 "thumbnail": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/snyvQ9COmb8/maxresdefault.jpg",
 "description": "#ai #generativeai #design \n\nEpisode 5 of Dream Logic features our first guest, Greg Hochmuth, who describes the seductive, infinite flow of AI-generated imagery, and what happens when it stops feeling magical. As both an artist and creative technologist, he brings a rare perspective on the immersive pull of the medium, the exhaustion that follows, and the moment when mystery gives way to math.\n\nPlease share with the curious.\n\nCreated by Kirby Ferguson and Karin Fyrhie.\n\nGreg Hochmuth\nhttps://grex.nyc/\n \nMusic: “Purple Punch” by Salamanda\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dCrUbUpcvQo\n\n...\n\nDrem Logic: Exploring the horizons of creative work\n\nDream Logic is something different from me. A collaboration with my pal Karin Fyhrie, an attempt to do something different and hopefully beautiful in collaboration with AI. It’s the start of a conversation: musings, artist interviews, and long looks into the strange, evolving landscape of new creative tools.\n\nSeason 1 episodes drop bi-weekly. Please share with the curious.\n\nSubscribe to our Substack to stay up to date: https://kirbyandkarin.substack.com",
